SecPRBench results and case explorer, published 2026-10-22.

This repository contains research artifacts exported from the SecPRBench
benchmark and the accompanying paper, with source hashes and provenance.
It does not change the licenses or ownership of those artifacts.

Upstream code, commit diffs, source snippets, issue descriptions, and reference
material retain their respective project licenses and attribution. The task
viewer preserves project identity and pinned upstream source links. Saved model
outputs and third-party report text retain their applicable ownership and terms.

The benchmark source currently records author-owned licensing and citation
metadata as publication work. This results website does not invent a blanket
license grant, author list, DOI, or institutional endorsement.

Generated and public cryptographic test fixtures can appear in code and logs.
They are historical test material, not operational account credentials. Public
trajectory projections apply the redactions described in docs/TRAJECTORIES.md.
Original raw trajectories are excluded from Git and the published website.

React, Vite, Shiki, and other package dependencies retain their own licenses.
The design is original; SWE-bench and SEC-bench served as interaction references
and are not affiliated with or endorsing this website.
